# API Service Patterns

## Centralized API Service
- **Main Service**: [src/lib/api.ts](mdc:src/lib/api.ts) - Centralized API service with all endpoints
- **API Client**: [src/lib/api-client.ts](mdc:src/lib/api-client.ts) - HTTP client configuration
- **Token Manager**: [src/lib/token-manager.ts](mdc:src/lib/token-manager.ts) - Token management
- **Error Handler**: [src/lib/error-handler.ts](mdc:src/lib/error-handler.ts) - Error handling utilities

## API Service Usage
- **ALWAYS** use `apiService` from [src/lib/api.ts](mdc:src/lib/api.ts) for all API calls
- **NEVER** use `fetch` directly in components
- **NEVER** create duplicate API service instances
- Use the singleton pattern: `import { apiService } from '@/lib/api'`

## API Response Format
All API responses follow this structure:
```typescript
interface ApiResponse<T> {
  success: boolean;
  data: T;
  message: string;
  timestamp: string;
}
```

## Authentication
- Tokens are automatically managed by the API service
- Access tokens are stored in localStorage
- Token refresh is handled automatically on 401 responses
- Use `apiService.login()` for authentication
- Use `apiService.logout()` to clear tokens

## Error Handling
- API errors are automatically handled by the error handler
- Use try-catch blocks for custom error handling
- Check `response.success` before accessing `response.data`
- Display user-friendly error messages

## API Endpoints
- All endpoints are defined in `API_ENDPOINTS` constant
- Use endpoint constants instead of hardcoded strings
- Endpoints are versioned with `/api` prefix
- Base URL comes from `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` environment variable

## Request Patterns
```typescript
// Correct pattern
const response = await apiService.getUsers();
if (response.success) {
  setUsers(response.data);
}

// With error handling
try {
  const response = await apiService.getUsers();
  if (response.success) {
    setUsers(response.data);
  } else {
    console.error('Failed to fetch users:', response.message);
  }
} catch (error) {
  console.error('API error:', error);
}
```

## Query Parameters
- Use URLSearchParams for query strings
- Filter out undefined/null/empty values
- Convert all values to strings

## File Downloads
- Use `apiService.downloadRejectionReport()` pattern for file downloads
- Set proper Accept headers (e.g., 'text/csv')
- Return Blob objects for downloads

## Token Management
- Tokens are automatically included in request headers
- Token refresh happens automatically
- Logout clears all tokens
- Never manually manipulate tokens in components

## Common Mistakes
- ❌ DON'T: Use fetch directly
- ❌ DON'T: Create new API service instances
- ❌ DON'T: Hardcode API endpoints
- ❌ DON'T: Manually manage tokens
- ✅ DO: Use apiService singleton
- ✅ DO: Use API_ENDPOINTS constants
- ✅ DO: Handle errors properly
- ✅ DO: Check response.success before using data
